{"title":"Should USG support a 50-year mortgage?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/927393773/0/marginalrevolution~Should-USG-support-a-year-mortgage.html","date":1762634855000,"content":"<p>More “affordability” from Trump!?  From GPT-5:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p>Broad, government‑backed 50‑year mortgages would likely <em>lower monthly payments</em> but <em>raise house prices</em>, <em>slow equity build‑up (and raise default risk in downturns)</em>, and <em>increase interest‑rate risk in the financial system</em>. As a general affordability policy for the U.S., that’s a poor trade‑off. If used at all, a 50‑year term should be tightly targeted (e.g., to loan <strong>modifications</strong> or to <strong>newly built</strong> homes only), not adopted wholesale for new purchases…</p>\r\n<p>In the short run, <strong>sellers</strong> and <strong>incumbent owners</strong> capture much of the benefit via higher sale prices; <strong>first‑time buyers</strong> face higher entry prices…</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://chatgpt.com/share/690fac37-cba8-8010-87e3-b9d0916cea88\" target=\"_blank\">the whole answer</a>.  Albania has the right idea!</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/11/should-usg-support-a-50-year-mortgage.html\">Should USG support a 50-year mortgage?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/927393773/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/927393773/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/927393773/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pint